From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Experto Boot Armbian H5 <agent@multica.local>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi_mmc: Force SPL MMC frequency to 25MHz to prevent HS hangs

High-speed SD cards can hang the sunxi_mmc driver in SPL on some boards
when switching to high-speed mode. Force f_max to 25MHz in SPL to keep
all cards in default speed mode during the critical SPL phase.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
index a111111111..b222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -699,6 +699,10 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	cfg->f_min = 400000;
 	cfg->f_max = 52000000;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SPL_BUILD
+	cfg->f_max = 25000000;
+#endif
+
 	cfg->b_max = CONFIG_SYS_MMC_MAX_BLK_COUNT;
 
 	upriv->mmc = &priv->mmc;
